#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:9
msgid "Decide how to internationalize and sync the README"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:13
msgid ""
"The project README (`README.md`, at the repo root) is English-only today."
" It is a Markdown file distinct from the Sphinx ReadTheDocs documentation"
" ([ADR-0008](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/439)) and "
"the Slidev talk deck ([ADR-0006](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/issues/442), [ADR-0003](0003-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-"
"slidev-deck.md)), so it needs its own internationalization strategy "
"rather than reusing Sphinx gettext or `slidev-addon-i18nb`. Issue "
"[#444](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/444) captures "
"the user-facing need to internationalize the README (e.g. JA, zh_CN, es) "
"and keep translations in sync automatically, so non-English-speaking "
"users can understand the project without a language barrier and "
"translations never go stale when the English README changes. GitHub "
"renders localized READMEs via `README.<lang>.md` files at the repo root "
"and shows a language switcher automatically, and "
"[#293](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/293) is aligning"
" the README with the [Standard Readme](https://github.com/RichardLitt"
"/standard-readme) specification — so the i18n structure must preserve "
"that layout in every language. The repo already enforces the Standard "
"Readme spec on `README.md` through a [`standard-"
"readme`](https://github.com/tkoyama010/standard-readme-pre-commit) pre-"
"commit hook. Which README i18n + sync strategy should we adopt so that "
"translations are GitHub-native, layout-consistent, and drift is detected "
"automatically?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:17
msgid ""
"**English is the authoritative source of truth**: The English `README.md`"
" is the source; every `README.<lang>.md` is derived from it. A localized "
"README never leads the English README in content. This is a knock-out "
"criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:18
msgid ""
"**Compatibility with GitHub's native `README.<lang>.md` rendering**: "
"GitHub renders `README.<lang>.md` files at the repo root and shows an "
"automatic language switcher. The solution must produce real, committed "
"`README.<lang>.md` files so the native switcher works with no custom UI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:19
msgid ""
"**Preserving the [Standard Readme](https://github.com/RichardLitt"
"/standard-readme) layout in every language**: "
"[#293](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/293) is aligning"
" `README.md` with the Standard Readme specification. Every localized "
"README must preserve the same section/heading structure so the spec holds"
" across languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:20
msgid ""
"**Detecting structural drift**: A translation that is missing or adds "
"sections, or whose headings diverge from the English README, must be "
"surfaced automatically — not left for a reviewer to spot by eye."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:21
msgid ""
"**Detecting content drift**: When the English `README.md` is updated, a "
"translation that is not regenerated or updated must be flagged "
"automatically, so stale translations cannot silently persist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:22
msgid ""
"**Automatic vs. manual sync; CI enforcement vs. PR-review-only**: The "
"project favours automated, verifiable enforcement over reliance on "
"reviewer vigilance, consistent with the pre-commit + CI pattern already "
"used throughout the repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:23
msgid ""
"**Zero-cost / GitHub-native tooling**: Per the drivers in [ADR-0003](0003"
"-decide-how-to-internationalize-the-slidev-deck.md) and "
"[ADR-0006](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/442), the "
"baseline must not require paid external services, API keys, or accounts "
"beyond what is already in the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:24
msgid ""
"**Minimal maintenance burden for a single-maintainer open-source "
"project**: The solution must be maintainable by one person; it should not"
" introduce a heavy build pipeline or a tool that demands ongoing "
"babysitting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:25
msgid ""
"**Consistency with ADR-0008 ([#439](https://github.com/tkoyama010"
"/pyvista-wasm/issues/439), ReadTheDocs i18n) and ADR-0006 "
"([#442](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/442), slide "
"locale sync)**: The README strategy should reuse the same drift-detection"
" philosophy where sensible, so the project has one coherent i18n-sync "
"story across docs, slides, and README."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:27
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:29
msgid ""
"**EN-authoritative with CI structural-parity check** — a script or pre-"
"commit hook comparing section/heading structure between `README.md` and "
"each `README.<lang>.md`, failing CI if they differ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:30
msgid ""
"**EN-authoritative with CI structural-parity + stale-translation check** "
"— also flags localized READMEs not updated after the English README "
"changes, via git-history/commit-date comparison"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:31
msgid ""
"**EN-authoritative with automated translation GitHub Action** — an LLM- "
"or API-based Action that opens a PR regenerating `README.<lang>.md` on "
"every English README change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:32
msgid ""
"**Dual-maintenance with no enforcement** — status quo; rely on PR review "
"to keep translations in sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:33
msgid ""
"**Single-source-of-truth with build-time locale generation** — one "
"`README.md` source plus a build step producing per-language files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:35
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:37
msgid ""
"Chosen option: **\"EN-authoritative with CI structural-parity + stale-"
"translation check\"**, because it is the only option that satisfies every"
" decision driver simultaneously — it keeps English as the authoritative "
"source, produces real committed `README.<lang>.md` files so GitHub's "
"native language switcher works, enforces the Standard Readme "
"section/heading structure across languages via structural parity, "
"surfaces both structural drift and content (stale-translation) drift "
"automatically, runs as zero-cost GitHub Actions plus a pre-commit hook "
"(no paid services or API keys), imposes minimal burden on a single "
"maintainer, and reuses the same drift-detection philosophy as ADR-0008 "
"and ADR-0006. Translations are authored manually by contributors; CI "
"flags drift rather than generating translations, so human judgement stays"
" in the loop and no external dependency is introduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:39
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:41
msgid ""
"Good, because GitHub's native `README.<lang>.md` rendering and automatic "
"language switcher work with no custom UI — the localized files are real "
"Markdown at the repo root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:42
msgid ""
"Good, because the structural-parity check guarantees every localized "
"README preserves the Standard Readme section/heading structure, so "
"[#293](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/293) alignment "
"holds across languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:43
msgid ""
"Good, because the stale-translation check surfaces content drift "
"automatically — a localized README not updated after an English README "
"change is flagged in CI, so stale translations cannot pass silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:44
msgid ""
"Good, because the checks run both as a pre-commit hook (fast local "
"feedback before push) and a CI workflow (enforcement on every PR), "
"matching the repo's existing quality-control pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:45
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and GitHub-native — a small stdlib-only "
"script invoked by GitHub Actions and pre-commit, with no paid services, "
"API keys, or external accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:46
msgid ""
"Good, because manual translation keeps human judgement in the loop and "
"introduces no LLM/API dependency or generated-PR review load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:47
msgid ""
"Bad, because translations are not generated automatically, so a "
"contributor must manually update each `README.<lang>.md` when the English"
" README changes; the stale-translation check reminds them but does not do"
" the work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:48
msgid ""
"Bad, because the structural-parity check compares structure, not "
"translation quality — a correctly-structured but poorly translated README"
" passes the check, so translation quality still relies on PR review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:49
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the stale-translation check uses git commit dates, which"
" can produce false positives if an English README change is cosmetic "
"(e.g. a badge URL) and does not require translation; contributors dismiss"
" these by touching the localized file or the check's allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:51
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:53
msgid "Compliance with this decision will be confirmed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:55
msgid ""
"At least one localized README (e.g. `README.ja.md`) exists at the repo "
"root alongside `README.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:56
msgid ""
"GitHub renders the language switcher on the repository page and selecting"
" a language displays the corresponding `README.<lang>.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:57
msgid ""
"Each `README.<lang>.md` follows the [Standard "
"Readme](https://github.com/RichardLitt/standard-readme) layout, verified "
"by the existing `standard-readme` pre-commit hook passing on every README"
" file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:58
msgid ""
"A CI workflow file (e.g. `.github/workflows/readme-i18n-check.yml`) "
"exists and passes, invoking the drift-detection script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:59
msgid ""
"The structural-parity check compares the heading/section structure of "
"`README.md` against each `README.<lang>.md` and fails on divergence "
"(missing, extra, or renamed sections/headings)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:60
msgid ""
"The stale-translation check flags any `README.<lang>.md` whose last "
"commit predates the latest `README.md` change, and fails CI until the "
"translation is updated or explicitly allowlisted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:61
msgid ""
"The drift-detection script has no third-party runtime dependencies "
"(Python stdlib only) or reuses tooling already present in the repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:62
msgid ""
"The translation and sync workflow is documented in `CONTRIBUTING.md`, "
"including how to add a new language and how to resolve a stale-"
"translation failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:63
msgid ""
"The check also runs as a pre-commit hook so drift is caught locally "
"before a push."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:65
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:67
msgid ""
"EN-authoritative with CI structural-parity check — compare "
"section/heading structure, fail on divergence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:69
msgid ""
"A zero-dependency script parses the headings/sections of `README.md` and "
"each `README.<lang>.md` and fails if the structure differs. Runs in CI "
"and/or as a pre-commit hook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:71
msgid ""
"Good, because it keeps English authoritative and catches structural drift"
" (missing, extra, or renamed sections) automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:72
msgid ""
"Good, because it preserves the Standard Readme layout across languages — "
"every localized README must mirror the English section structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:73
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and GitHub-native: a stdlib-only script in "
"GitHub Actions, no paid services or API keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:74
msgid ""
"Good, because it is low maintenance for a single maintainer — one small "
"script, no build pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:75
msgid ""
"Good, because it is consistent with the drift-detection philosophy of "
"ADR-0008 and ADR-0006."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:76
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it can run as both a pre-commit hook and a CI workflow, "
"giving fast local feedback and PR enforcement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:77
msgid ""
"Bad, because it detects only structural drift, not content drift — a "
"translation can be stale (English README updated, translation not) yet "
"structurally identical, so it passes the check silently. This fails the "
"content-drift decision driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:79
msgid ""
"EN-authoritative with CI structural-parity + stale-translation check — "
"also flag translations not updated after the English README changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:81
msgid ""
"Builds on the structural-parity check by also comparing git history: if "
"`README.md` was committed after a given `README.<lang>.md`, the "
"translation is flagged as stale and CI fails until it is updated or "
"explicitly allowlisted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:83
msgid ""
"Good, because it satisfies every decision driver: English authoritative, "
"GitHub-native `README.<lang>.md` rendering, Standard Readme layout "
"preserved, structural drift detected, content drift detected, zero-cost, "
"low maintenance, and consistent with ADR-0008/ADR-0006."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:84
msgid ""
"Good, because it catches both kinds of drift — a localized README that "
"diverges in structure or that falls behind the English README is surfaced"
" automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:85
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and GitHub-native: a stdlib-only script "
"using `git log`/commit dates, run in GitHub Actions and pre-commit, with "
"no paid services or API keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:86
msgid ""
"Good, because it keeps human judgement in the loop — translations are "
"manual, so no LLM/API dependency and no generated-PR review load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:87
msgid ""
"Good, because it is low maintenance for a single maintainer — one small "
"script covering both checks, no build pipeline or external service to "
"babysit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:88
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the stale-translation check uses commit dates and can "
"false-flag cosmetic English changes (e.g. a badge URL); an allowlist or a"
" trivial touch of the localized file dismisses these."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:89
msgid ""
"Bad, because it does not generate translations — a contributor must still"
" update each `README.<lang>.md` by hand; the check reminds them but does "
"not do the work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:90
msgid ""
"Bad, because it does not assess translation quality — a correctly "
"structured but poorly translated README passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:92
msgid ""
"EN-authoritative with automated translation GitHub Action — LLM/API-based"
" Action opens a PR regenerating README.<lang>.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:94
msgid ""
"A GitHub Action watches `README.md` changes and uses an LLM or "
"translation API to regenerate each `README.<lang>.md`, opening a PR with "
"the result for review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:96
msgid ""
"Good, because it eliminates manual translation effort for the initial "
"generation and reduces content drift — the Action regenerates "
"translations on every English change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:97
#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:124
msgid ""
"Good, because it keeps English authoritative and can produce committed "
"`README.<lang>.md` files for GitHub's native switcher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:98
msgid ""
"Good, because content drift is largely eliminated — the Action runs on "
"every English README change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:99
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it can produce committed `README.<lang>.md` files, but "
"the generated Markdown may not exactly preserve the Standard Readme "
"layout without prompt engineering and review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:100
msgid ""
"Bad, because it violates the zero-cost / GitHub-native driver — LLM and "
"translation APIs require paid API keys or accounts beyond what is in the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:101
msgid ""
"Bad, because every generated PR must be reviewed by a human for accuracy "
"and layout, adding a recurring review load that is not \"minimal "
"maintenance\" for a single maintainer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:102
msgid ""
"Bad, because LLM translations can hallucinate or drop content (e.g. code "
"blocks, badge URLs), so structural-parity is not guaranteed without an "
"additional check — meaning this option needs the structural-parity check "
"on top anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:103
msgid ""
"Bad, because it is inconsistent with the drift-detection philosophy of "
"ADR-0008/ADR-0006, which favour detection over automatic generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:105
msgid "Dual-maintenance with no enforcement — status quo, rely on PR review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:107
msgid ""
"Localized READMEs are maintained by hand with no automated checks; "
"keeping them in sync is left to reviewer vigilance during PR review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:109
msgid ""
"Good, because it requires no tooling, scripts, or CI workflow — zero "
"implementation effort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:110
msgid "Good, because it is zero-cost and introduces no dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:111
msgid ""
"Good, because it is low effort to start — a contributor simply adds a "
"`README.<lang>.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:112
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it is the default state of a repo with localized READMEs"
" and no automation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:113
msgid ""
"Bad, because it fails the structural-drift and content-drift drivers — "
"nothing detects a missing section or a stale translation, so drift "
"accumulates silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:114
msgid ""
"Bad, because it fails the CI-enforcement driver — reliance on reviewer "
"vigilance is exactly what the project's pre-commit + CI pattern exists to"
" avoid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:115
msgid ""
"Bad, because it is inconsistent with ADR-0008/ADR-0006, which both "
"automate drift detection rather than relying on review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:116
msgid ""
"Bad, because for a single maintainer there often is no other reviewer, so"
" \"rely on PR review\" reduces to \"rely on the same person remembering "
"every language,\" which does not scale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:118
msgid ""
"Single-source-of-truth with build-time locale generation — one README "
"source, build step produces per-language files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:120
msgid ""
"A single source (e.g. a template or a structured source file with "
"translatable strings) is built into `README.md` and each "
"`README.<lang>.md` at build time, so all languages share one structure by"
" construction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:122
msgid ""
"Good, because structural drift is impossible by construction — every "
"language is generated from the same template, so headings and sections "
"always match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:123
msgid ""
"Good, because content drift is eliminated — regeneration from the source "
"keeps every language current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:125
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the generated `README.<lang>.md` files are build "
"artifacts that must be committed for GitHub to render them, which is "
"unusual (committed artifacts) and can cause noisy diffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:126
msgid ""
"Bad, because it violates the minimal-maintenance driver — it introduces a"
" build pipeline (template engine, string store, generation script) that a"
" single maintainer must build and maintain, far heavier than a drift-"
"detection script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:127
msgid ""
"Bad, because it conflicts with the existing `standard-readme` pre-commit "
"hook, which lints `README.md` directly; if `README.md` becomes a "
"generated artifact, the hook must be reworked to lint the source or the "
"generated output, adding complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:128
msgid ""
"Bad, because contributors edit a template/string store rather than "
"`README.md` itself, which is unfamiliar and raises the contribution "
"barrier for a simple README fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0007-decide-how-to-internationalize-and-sync-the-readme.md:129
msgid ""
"Bad, because it is only partially zero-cost / GitHub-native — the "
"generation tooling must be added and run in CI, adding build time and "
"workflow complexity beyond the stdlib-only script of the drift-detection "
"options."
msgstr ""

